From 814d423d69c9beec6041ed34f50496ae93b80cc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:16:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] libdocument: optionally link the document backends into
 the programs

-Dbuiltin_backends=true builds each backend as a static library, compiled
with its register_atril_backend() renamed ev_builtin_<Module>_register(),
and links it into atril, atril-previewer and atril-thumbnailer. A table
generated from the backends' .atril-backend files
(backend/ev-builtin-backends.py: Module, Resident, TypeDescription,
MimeType) lists them; the backends manager adds its entries before it
scans the backends directory (a module of the same name there is then
ignored, and a missing directory is no longer an error), and an EvModule
made by ev_module_new_builtin() calls the register function instead of
g_module_open(). libdocument refers to the table weakly: a program linked
without it has no built-in backends.

For systems without dynamic loading (a fully static Phoenix-RTOS build).
Only the pdf backend is converted; configure stops if another backend is
enabled together with builtin_backends. The default (false) builds
exactly what it did.
